# Password input

Use the native password field and a deliberate show-or-hide control when a password is required.

These are civica reference implementations for component authors. They do not replace native Home Assistant behaviour or demonstrate a connection to a live home.

## When to use it

Use it for an actual password entry task. Distinguish creating a password from entering an existing one through the autocomplete value.

## When not to use it

Do not use a password field for a one-time code, device address or arbitrary identifier. Do not build a second login flow around the theme: preserve Home Assistant authentication and credential handling.

## Home Assistant adaptation

These examples contain no stored credentials and do not authenticate. In production, allow password managers and paste. Keep the password hidden initially and return the input type to password before submission. Do not change the account’s password policy through presentation code.

## Accessibility and behaviour

Give the toggle a specific accessible name and a relationship to its input. Disable spellcheck and automatic capitalisation for exposed text. Use current-password or new-password as appropriate. Avoid an unnecessary second confirmation field.

